    "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n## What does this PR do?\n\nFix CUDA graph capture in `torch_chunk_gated_delta_rule` when no initial recurrent state is supplied. The existing `torch.zeros(...).to(value)` allocates an unpinned CPU tensor and copies it to CUDA during capture, raising `CUDA error: operation not permitted when stream is capturing`.\n\nAllocate the state directly with `value.new_zeros(...)`, preserving its shape, device, and FP32 dtype. The supplied-initial-state path and recurrence are unchanged.\n\nAdd 16 regression cases covering FP32/BF16, sequence lengths 64/65, supplied/absent initial state, and optional final state. Each captures forward and backward, compares changed-input replays bit-exactly with eager outputs and gradients, and verifies repeated replay.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Reproduced the original failure with NeMo 26.10 RC5 on 8 GB300 GPUs using `qwen35_text_9b_pretrain_8gpu_gb200_bf16_deterministic_config`: three finite training iterations, then failure during TE graph capture. Original vocabulary 248077, global batch 128, microbatch 2, sequence length 4096.\n- In the same RC5 stack, the candidate passed 16 isolated raw CUDA graph cases and four Transformer Engine `make_graphed_callables` checks, including forward/backward, eager parity, changed inputs, and repeated replay.\n- Full-model validation on 8 GB300 GPUs with the candidate and the original recipe passed TE graph capture and completed all 10 training iterations with finite, unskipped losses (10th loss: 0.2513471246). Final validation/test evaluation also completed; all eight ranks returned successfully and the batch exited 0. The stock installed dependencies and exact Bridge commit are retained; only this function's allocation expression is replaced in memory after an exact-source check.\n- Kernel determinism coverage check, Black, isort, pylint, Ruff, and `git diff --check` passed. The `autoformat.sh` wrapper requires Git >=2.31; this workstation has 2.25.1, so its tools were run directly. Advisory mypy checks remain limited by unavailable workstation GPU dependencies.\n- The full pytest module has not been run on current main. All 16 cases of the new regression function passed when exercised directly in the RC5 GPU validation job.\n\nRC5 MCore: `e30d863a6d82a3c45f2d71355dc73fbf5610967b`. Bridge: `3b91885d5411e4a2f198066c88eb2104da99b12f`. The current-main function and the RC5 function are identical before this one-line change.\n\n## Pre-checks\n\n- [x] Added relevant unit and bit-exact determinism tests; the existing manifest already registers this source and test file.\n- [ ] Added a functional test to CI (manual full-model training and final evaluation passed).\n- [ ] Full current-main pytest/CI validation.\n\nRequested release targets: NeMo 26.10 / MCore 0.20.0.\n",
